ta's advantages are substantial: a D+5 district lean, a long incumbency marked by bipartisan work on water and agriculture, and a lopsided money race, with roughly $658,000 on hand against about $6,500 for Kyle Kirkland. Kirkland, a farmer campaigning on water management and rising costs, has run a low-funded race with essentially no outside support. Costa's centrist record, including a U.S. Chamber endorsement and federal water infrastructure funding, blunts Republican opportunities in a district that can swing in presidential years.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9799, "margin": 14.05}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9726, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9754, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9684, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9588, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.957, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9737, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9821, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9693, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9851, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.977, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9684, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9786, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9724, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9732, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9813, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9768, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9729, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.981, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.9751, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.9807, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.9785, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.9634, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.9721, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-16", "p_dem": 0.9691, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-17",